@startuml state-job-run
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: a run is one Celery task execution of a job; its state comes only from
'       facts (the publish hook, Celery events, the sweeper), never from a client,
'       and one precedence rule keeps late or duplicate events from moving it back.
' Kind: UML state machine diagram, proposal (IP-031 rev. 2). Scope: JobRun (table
'       job_protocols). Omitted: how a run's outcome moves its job (state-job).
' Source: apps/tasks/ledger.py, apps/tasks/maintenance.py (2026-11-14).
' =============================================================================

title Job run state machine: facts only, one precedence rule (proposal, 2026-11-14)

state "queued" as queued : written before the send\n(publish hook / dispatcher)
state "received" as received : task-received
state "started" as started : task-started\nattempts + 1
state "retrying" as retrying : task-retried\n(Celery self.retry)
state "succeeded" as succeeded : task-succeeded\nresult, runtime
state "failed" as failed : task-failed\nerror, traceback
state "revoked" as revoked : task-revoked, or cancelled\nbefore a worker took it\n<b>final</b>
state "rejected" as rejected : task-rejected
state "lost" as lost : sweeper: no event past\nthe time limit (+ grace)

[*] -[$accent()]-> queued : <b>before_task_publish</b>
queued -[$accent()]-> received : <b>task-received</b>
received -[$accent()]-> started : <b>task-started</b>
started -[$accent()]-> succeeded : <b>task-succeeded</b>
started --> failed : task-failed
started --> retrying : task-retried
retrying --> received : task-received\n(retry delivered)
received --> rejected : task-rejected
queued --> revoked : job cancelled\n(revoke)
received --> revoked : task-revoked
started --> revoked : task-revoked\n(terminated)
queued --> lost : sweeper:\nno event for 48 h
started --> lost : sweeper:\nno event past time limit
received --> lost : sweeper
succeeded --> received : newer task-received\n(redelivery, stable task id)
failed --> received : newer task-received
lost --> started : newer task-started\n(the event was only late)

legend bottom left
  |= Rule |= |
  | older than last_event_at | event is history only (job_events), no state change |
  | revoked | final: nothing moves it |
  | other final states | reopen only on a newer task-received / task-started |
  | queued | only from nothing; a late task-sent never moves a run back |
endlegend

caption Runs are facts. They feed their job's state machine: queued/received → job queued, started/retrying → running,\nsucceeded → succeeded, failed/lost/rejected → failed or pending (retry policy), revoked → cancelled.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/state-job-run.puml
@enduml
